# Configure database indices.
# Variables: none
#
# This uses "replace" with a complete, explicit index policy rather than "add".
#
# The RPM-shipped configuration already defines olcDbIndex values for {2}mdb:
#
#   olcDbIndex: objectClass eq,pres
#   olcDbIndex: ou,cn,mail,surname,givenname eq,pres,sub
#
# Adding a second definition for the same attribute is rejected outright with
# "duplicate index definition for attr <name>", which makes the whole modify
# fail atomically. Because that failure was previously swallowed by "|| true",
# the image shipped with whatever indices the RPM happened to define - notably
# without an entryCSN or entryUUID index, which syncrepl searches on constantly.
#
# Attribute names in an index definition ARE validated against the loaded
# schema, and the only schema loaded by default is core.schema. This is why
# memberOf is NOT indexed here: the memberOf attribute type does not exist
# until the memberof overlay is loaded, and overlays are configured *after*
# this step, so listing it fails with
#   index attribute "memberOf" undefined
#
# If you enable ENABLE_MEMBEROF=true and query on memberOf heavily, add the
# index after startup (the overlay will have defined the attribute by then):
#
#   docker exec -i <container> ldapmodify -Y EXTERNAL -H ldapi:/// <<'EOF'
#   dn: olcDatabase={2}mdb,cn=config
#   changetype: modify
#   add: olcDbIndex
#   olcDbIndex: memberOf eq
#   EOF
#
# ALIASES of the same attribute DO collide. core.schema defines
# "2.5.4.4 NAME ( 'sn' 'surname' )", so listing both sn and surname triggers
# "duplicate index definition for attr surname". Use exactly one name per
# attribute type: sn (not sn + surname), givenName (not givenName + gn),
# uid (not uid + userid), mail (not mail + rfc822Mailbox).
#
# This step runs on first initialisation, while the database is still empty, so
# replacing the index set does not require reindexing existing data.
dn: olcDatabase={2}mdb,cn=config
changetype: modify
replace: olcDbIndex
olcDbIndex: objectClass eq
olcDbIndex: ou,cn,sn,givenName pres,eq,sub
olcDbIndex: uid pres,eq
olcDbIndex: mail pres,eq,sub
olcDbIndex: member eq
olcDbIndex: entryCSN eq
olcDbIndex: entryUUID eq
